The '''Starship Graveyard''', also known as the '''Graveyard of Giants''' or '''Graveyard of Ships''', was a wide desert area on the [[planet]] [[Jakku]] that took its name because of the wreckage of "giant" ships accumulated on its dunes as a result of the [[Battle of Jakku]].

==History==
[[File:JakkuLitterbugs-TFAT2.png|thumb|left|300px|The ''Inflictor''{{'s}} wreckage in the Graveyard of Giants.]]
One [[Standard year|year]] after the [[Battle of Endor]], the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[New Republic]] fought a [[Battle of Jakku|battle]] on [[Jakku]], during which damaged [[starship]]s of both factions crash landed on the terrain, littering the landscape with debris and dangerous volatiles like fuel and coolant.<ref name="Survival" /> Among the wreckage of huge warships were the ''[[Inflictor]]''<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> and the ''[[Ravager]]''.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> [[New Republic Defense Force|Republic infantry]] attempted to strike a decisive attack against the [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] defending their [[Imperial research base|weapons facility]].<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> In one section of the graveyard, the [[Crackle]], the sandy terrain had been turned to [[glass]] from the heat of a crash.<ref name="Before the Awakening" />

[[Pilot]] [[Taka Jamoreesa]] flew a [[Resistance transport]] through the graveyard at one point.<ref name="Hot Shots and Aces">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/hot-shots-aces-ii-resistance-overview|text=Hot Shots and Aces II Resistance Overview|date=2022-11-16}}</ref> The [[35 ABY]]<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref> [[Uprising on Jakku|uprising]] against the [[First Order]] added at least one [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] to the wreckage littering this area.<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
"Graveyard of Giants" is one of the two maps introduced in the free ''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]'' downloadable content called "Battle of Jakku," which was released on [[December 8]], [[2015]].

The Graveyard first appeared in ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Immersive 360 Experience]]'', a promotional video created exclusively for [[Wikipedia:Facebook|Facebook]].<ref name="TFA 360">{{Facebook|username=StarWars|url=StarWars/videos/1030579940326940|name=''[[Star Wars]]''|archivedate=20160219052927}}</ref>

